# Colorectal Cancer miRNA Analysis

This project compares two computational methods, miRDeep2 and
miRge3.0, for identifying known and novel microRNAs associated
with colorectal cancer.

 Research Question
How do computational methods: miRDeep2 and miRge3.0 differ in identifying known and
novel microRNAs in colorectal cancer?

 Dataset
NCBI Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO): GSE43550

Focus
The project focuses on miR-195-5p, a microRNA associated with
the regulation of cell proliferation in colorectal cancer.

 Computational Methods
- miRDeep2
- miRge3.0
- Cutadapt

Research proposal and computational analysis in development.
